omp-web (0.3.9) jammy; urgency=medium

  * session-title: rewrite the browser-facing title-summarization prompts to
    always answer in Simplified Chinese, place any recognized GitHub issue
    number annotation at the front of the title instead of appending it as
    a suffix, and target roughly 100 Hanzi or fewer (raised the hard
    truncation ceiling from 120 to 150 chars as headroom for the longest
    annotation prefixes, not a new target length) (`lib/session-title.ts`,
    `lib/title-annotations.ts`, `components/HomeCalendar.tsx`).
  * postinst: overwrite the SDK's own bundled default title-generation
    prompts (`title-system.md`, `title-marker-instruction.md` under
    `@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent`) with the same Chinese/prefix/~100-char
    house style, on both the fresh-install and upgrade/reinstall overlay
    paths. This is purely defensive: every omp-web code path that generates
    a title already passes its own `customSystemPrompt`, so these SDK
    defaults are not read today and this step changes no currently
    observable behavior — it only guards a future code path that might
    omit `customSystemPrompt`.
  * docs: remove the stale `docs/release.md` and `docs/fleet-deployment.md`
    (superseded by `docs/plans/2026-08-20-omp-web-release-pipeline.md` and
    `AGENTS.md`'s deployment topology); the still-active npm-publish steps
    from `docs/release.md` were inlined into
    `.claude/skills/github-release/SKILL.md` so that skill remains
    self-contained.

